description:
Join us for an afternoon at the frontier of health behavior change. Across three hours, leaders from architecture, AI, insurance, and behavioral science will explore how environmental engineering, AI coaching, behavioral design, and data analytics converge to make healthy choices effortless — and lasting.

Our speakers include 
Steph Habif, Head of AI Health Coaching, Google; 
Bruce Ling, Senior Research Scientist, Stanford University School of Medicine; 
Emi Kiyota, Founder of Ibasho and Associate Professor of NUS; 
Kristen Berman, CEO & Co-Founder Irrational Labs; 
Tak Miyata, Founder and GP Scrum Ventures 
and many more! 
Please confirm the attached flyer for full agenda and speaker list.

This event is a part of #SFTechWeek—a week of events hosted by VCs and startups to bring together the tech ecosystem. Learn more at www.tech-week.com.
